#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060748} :activity/id #uuid "a395b4a3-cd2d-5496-be63-828e164fb8a3" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049842 :topic/id #uuid "18160fcf-bc16-5973-b12d-9d8b5753934f" :topic/math-academy-id 240} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060748 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060958 :tutorial/content "A **partition** of a set $A$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $A$ where every element of $A$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nIn other words, none of the subsets can be the null set $(\\emptyset),$ and every element of $A$ must be contained in one *and only one* subset.\n\nFor example, the following collections of subsets of $X=\\{1, 2, 3, 4, 5\\}$ are all partitions:\n\n- $X_1 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2\\}, \\{ 3, 4 \\}, \\{5\\} \\}$\n\n- $X_2 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$\n\n- $X_3 = \\{ \\{ 1, 3\\}, \\{ 2\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$\n\n- $X_4 = \\{ \\{ 1, 4, 5\\}, \\{ 2, 3\\} \\}$\n\n- $X_5 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2, 3, 4\\}, \\{5\\} \\}$\n\nHowever, the following collections are *not* partitions:\n\n- $X_6 = \\{ \\{ 1\\}, \\{ 3, 4 \\}, \\{5\\} \\}$ - the number $2$ is not included in any subset\n\n- $X_7 = \\{ \\emptyset, \\{ 1, 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$ - includes $\\emptyset$\n\n- $X_8 = \\{ \\{ 1, 3\\}, \\{ 2, 3\\}, \\{4, 5\\} \\}$ - the number $3$ is included in two different subsets\n\n- $X_9 = \\{ \\{ 1, 2 \\}, \\{ 2, 3\\} \\}$ - missing $4$ and $5,$ and $2$ is included in two different subsets\n\n- $X_{10} = \\{ 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 \\}$ - this not a collection of subsets" :tutorial/id #uuid "7c175282-8683-5a55-a872-02bbd19be4f5" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4252 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "f50a4e80-5c54-5d58-ab17-5ed548aaeb19" :step/math-academy-id 25815 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060750}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060749 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059812 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059615 :question/id #uuid "6e647